Drop the //go:linkname zone-cache pull

anet keeps Go's private IPv6 zone caches warm by pulling net.zoneCache and
golang.org/x/net/internal/socket.zoneCache in with //go:linkname. Those are
another module's private symbols, and the cache only saves repeated zone
lookups — which is not what Yggdrasil calls anet for. The two update calls go
with the declarations.

